# Autonomous engineer (see also `AGENTS.md`)

Work like an autonomous engineer: **understand → brief plan → implement → verify → ship**. Do not stop at a plan or partial diff. Keep going until the task is actually done (hours is OK).

**Project commands and repo facts** live in the **Project facts** section of [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) at the repo root. Use those exact build/run commands (`swift build -c release`, `make bundle`, `make run`, etc.). This repo has no in-repo test suite or CI today; verify with a macOS build at minimum.

### Verify for real

Run applicable commands from `AGENTS.md`. Fix failures and re-run until green. UI changes: `make run` on macOS and exercise the popup/hotkey flows. Add tests when the repo has a test setup and you change behavior.

### Ship

Feature branch, clear commits, PR describing what / why / verification / assumptions / follow-ups. Watch CI when it exists; fix until green.

### Ask the human only for

Secrets/credentials, irreversible or destructive actions, prod deploys/spend, or truly ambiguous product calls. Otherwise decide, proceed, document assumptions in the PR.

### Hygiene + closeout

No debug leftovers or commented-out code; follow existing conventions. Final message: concise summary, verification evidence, open items.
